Subject: [PATCH v13 7/8] jails/instances/lab-mail: Take posts for the
 lists.p7x.dev lists
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev
Change-Id: mxytnonnzulosvkynknsvqvvotnplwmv
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 21:55:08 +0000

The hub should carry lab@lists.p7x.dev and freebsd-ports@lists.p7x.dev
as well as lab-devel@p7x.dev. Mail to either of those addresses would
otherwise be refused at RCPT TO, so the client would drop the message
and it would reach no one.

- smtpd.conf's table list names all three addresses.
- The spec and README.org name them.
- A message to two list addresses lands once for each, since
  OpenSMTPD delivers each recipient separately. The spec says so,
  and that notmuch still shows it once.
---
change-id: mxytnonnzulosvkynknsvqvvotnplwmv

 jails/instances/lab-claude/README.org         |  3 ++-
 jails/instances/lab-mail/README.org           |  5 +++-
 .../dist/usr/local/etc/mail/smtpd.conf        |  8 +++---
 jails/instances/lab-mail/spec.org             | 27 +++++++++++--------
 4 files changed, 26 insertions(+), 17 deletions(-)

diff --git a/jails/instances/lab-claude/README.org b/jails/instances/lab-claude/README.org
